 22: /**
 23:  * The band relay. Every game socket is a peer; a peer that sends `start`
 24:  * becomes a performer, and each of their batches goes to every peer on the
 25:  * same map whose character can see them - the tracker already knows that
 26:  * from the server's own scope packets. Nothing here reaches the game
 27:  * server: `main.ts` hands band frames here instead of writing them to TCP.
 28:  *
 29:  * Bun-free and timer-free, with an injectable clock, so the tests drive it
 30:  * like `TrackedSession`. `main.ts` calls `sweep` on an interval.
 31:  *
 32:  * Limits are Space Station 14's (`BAND_LIMITS`). A malformed or oversized
 33:  * frame is dropped and counted as a strike; a sustained breach stops the
 34:  * performance, which tells every receiver and the performer, and starts a
 35:  * cooldown. Nothing a client sends can cost the proxy more than one
 36:  * decrypt, a few range checks and the sends it was going to do anyway.
 37:  */
